  "qualification": "Source review only. Owner execution reports are not inherited as independent reruns, clean-candidate qualification or HIL evidence.",
  "verified_invariants": [
    "Linux task admission rejects foreign TLS identities and nonrunning phases before its observer mutex; bootstrap ownership is callback-thread-local.",
    "All three official macro observers return actual kernel values. Combined return flags read system state and preemption state in one mutex snapshot.",
    "Successful attribute initialization, recursive-type setup and mutex initialization precede release publication; publication precedes timer pthread creation.",
    "Acquire readiness gates locking. The supported single-owner preinitialization path returns the actual initialization sentinel and pointer without accessing the uninitialized mutex.",
    "Each observer uses the official timed-retry lock and releases exactly its own recursive mutex depth without interrupt-control APIs.",
    "Early declarations use unsigned int consistently and a forward-declared struct TX_THREAD_STRUCT pointer; C and C++ linkage and both debug volatile declarations match kernel definitions.",
    "The scheduler retains its mutex through the selected-thread run acknowledgement and omits only the redundant timer-origin-independent suspend/resume pair; the ISR handshake remains.",
    "The suspend handler retains its full mask, acknowledgement and errno preservation, consumes only blocked SIGUSR2 with sigwait, and aborts invalid waits.",
    "Production and instrumented hosts use the same exact-source-derived overlays; no sanitizer suppression or raw-syscall bypass was introduced.",
    "Linux guards leave the Cortex-M observer implementation and source graph unchanged; the original vendor sources and Gitlink remain outside the owned patch.",
    "Reviewed test contracts cover foreign runtime/bootstrap rejection, actual port masking, cold no-lock observations, recursive depth preservation, real pending resume, complete signal-mask restoration and exact derivation boundaries."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Concurrent raw kernel calls during initialization and concurrent kernel entry are outside the supported single-bootstrap-owner contract.",
    "Individual observations and combined flags do not serialize the complete later preemption decision; upstream subsequent execute-pointer reads remain separate.",
    "GNU sigwait safety rationale is bound to the reviewed Linux glibc syscall/cancellation implementation and GCC 14.3.0 interceptor source, not a generic POSIX async-safety guarantee.",
    "Cancellation interrupting arbitrary executing product code retains the upstream caveat; supported adapter deletion targets completed or never-executed bootstrap tasks.",
    "This independent review did not execute normal, TSan, tool, ARM, style or physical checks and does not claim their outcomes."
  ],
